.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"3c8b011cd61bca510655ac3339ab544761a14e4107bc02f024a72e07efb0936d","compact":"b1c1e59056f11b26dd8037115a8b722e233f28cc600274cb332375ffa46bf674","nasal":"0ea516928e93377603ce95f2f014e6a58a359b9daa0182a321e12e97bea02d89"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-2-7","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":2,"verse":7,"english":"And with his senses centred on the study of the Vedas, that righteous-souled one, going to the hermitage, carried on austerities; but his religious rites were disturbed by certain girls. And daughters of sages and Pannagas and those of Rājarşis, as well as those of Apsarās, sporting, arrived at that quarter.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-2-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7002007","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7b35b0082b875b0a71733709261e9c1ca458b22544316956848f05e033cb8a38","compact":"8e291277324579984cf1de1323f4b7d4f81b856fabe2e76463bfb1b42edd8040","nasal":"51ad9148cabbb42a46c8c190169a2fbad277cbe51fb0d8327f6ec87b4408a548"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-2-8","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":2,"verse":8,"english":"And with his senses centred on the study of the Vedas, that righteous-souled one, going to the hermitage, carried on austerities; but his religious rites were disturbed by certain girls. And daughters of sages and Pannagas and those of Rājarşis, as well as those of Apsarās, sporting, arrived at that quarter.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.951,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-2-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7002008","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"be3d18d80d1197e7123798e0b76b31c7a9b301f26a913485ccbd611c1879c20d","compact":"fe26500c5df30c67f4b8ed2605980760816feaa24f9aea99bb4d76c83c161d18","nasal":"8f241f4134d568160fd9a71405e92c0d8e6c5b60199637e05cf109ca1ab1575f"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-2-9","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":2,"verse":9,"english":"And an account of every season being genial at that spot and also of the loveliness of the wood, the damsels, repairing to this place. ever disport there.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-2-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7002009","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"9511d2e98efd752636d154113ba081dfdf3eb557fd678fb117d27d028bf08998","compact":"513061000166b1e2378cca3d470b58f27e24227afd648ca396b2b4dc3b5b37eb","nasal":"5cba0d129d44c5310b16ed27241ff8cb526d5be8c1434a185c832bd5c3e82dee"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-2-10","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":2,"verse":10,"english":"And on account of the beauty of that region, those wenches, coming to where that twice-born one, Pulastya was, used to sing, to play on instruments, and to dance; and thus those blameless beauties disturbed the rites of that anchoret practising austerities. Thereat, the mighty ascetic, waxing wroth, said, ‘She that comes within my kin, shall conceive.' Hearing the words of the high-souled one, (the damsels), afraid of a Brāhamana's curse, ceased to to haunt that place. But Triņabindu's daughter had not heard anything of all this, and going to the asylum, she ranged it fearlessly.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.407,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-2-10","DUTT-7-2-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7002010","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"88037574fab5174592ecc2454debe57f30061294f27e8f107359565cf98c158c","compact":"4341efbd48fa5d0828170621b14a8510c352b1034e6af09fd3045065bf523300","nasal":"4341efbd48fa5d0828170621b14a8510c352b1034e6af09fd3045065bf523300"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-2-11","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":2,"verse":11,"english":"‘She that comes within my kin, shall conceive.' Hearing the words of the high-souled one, (the damsels), afraid of a Brāhamana's curse, ceased to to haunt that place. But Triņabindu's daughter had not heard anything of all this, and going to the asylum, she ranged it fearlessly.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.597,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-2-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7002011","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"34504306a8bbfeef028d9b23fcb2673a0db9586c1aaa6acb950be0cf0fc2a0f5","compact":"838125528ac55307519bef68ba80ed102dafc330c69aa1aad55dfe55f1078acf","nasal":"838125528ac55307519bef68ba80ed102dafc330c69aa1aad55dfe55f1078acf"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-2-12","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":2,"verse":12,"english":"‘She that comes within my kin, shall conceive.' Hearing the words of the high-souled one, (the damsels), afraid of a Brāhamana's curse, ceased to to haunt that place. But Triņabindu's daughter had not heard anything of all this, and going to the asylum, she ranged it fearlessly.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.833,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-2-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7002012","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d5429b50653644fa7986b62c25eea4486b2b59ae0e6592a4c00272bee3055691","compact":"1a612f35f67cf9ee3cb7e76e9d028c91af89819d792b7d589c6ce2a02afeba93","nasal":"29735a711a4ae1f7e3a5ae085681082d57f8fa57ddcabcb7794f11328837ea31"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-2-13","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":2,"verse":13,"english":"She did not see there any of her associates come to that spot. And at that time that exceedingly energetic and mighty sage, Prajāpati's son, with his soul sanctified through eticism, was engaged in the study of the Veda.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.547,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-2-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7002013","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"23c7d18e266a38526308d66e6267cdce5bed99fba7814550a7e26392871d590a","compact":"1a6d4a61e58feb04c267901a2388f376d5839b04055aff9f9278561367de11dd","nasal":"f5078f0618f70df34e9b7b4dadb0782b029ddbc7afeaa15c7ada0e88b6158f9a"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-2-14","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":2,"verse":14,"english":"Hearing the sounds of Vedic recitation, and seeing that storehouse of asceticism, she had her body turned pale, and signs of pregnancy displayed themselves.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.446,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-2-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7002014","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"d71a876c578b9e0920d33f8ef2403fe8852f9f57f2a475c3469806ffbfa6f58f","compact":"1f3c5d6f16fa6c7e28bbcd2cb2fac51278d4a3c88892cb4076434d9c609b34af","nasal":"a6b0211dd12086e3d03b5bc368e510873d5aef38eda2341af4ae390f78fe82e6"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-2-15","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":2,"verse":15,"english":"Seeing that evil befall her, she was wrought up with anxiety; and, understanding matters, she said, \"What is this?' And, going to her father's hermitage, stayed there.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.356,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-2-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7002015","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"33c3459e8968c3740df03877c6895a5ebf83bb9c5a30bbebe49c0cee7b006e22","compact":"0ca8bf4d521aaed53764b33424816bde05de4999127d5c4eea6a36844183f0f8","nasal":"0ca8bf4d521aaed53764b33424816bde05de4999127d5c4eea6a36844183f0f8"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-2-16","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":2,"verse":16,"english":"Seeing her in this condition, Triņabindu said, \"Wherefore is the person that you bear unlike what it used to be?'","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-2-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7002016","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"e9959bff3700b2c933c708320fe7827549149d50d988fb46662e65b68b655439","compact":"d58c1ca1e09e471f7bee2671a387ac33454c2d9ecce2b3e7549c2724ffc7e965","nasal":"9c17223b5772e0a443afd26a7e531274c13c7f93474ee889217bb69e6280d1b3"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-2-17","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":2,"verse":17,"english":"Thereat, in .woe-begone guise, with joined hands, his daughter replied to that one having asceticism for the riches, 'O father, cause know I none whereby I have come by this appearance.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.857,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-2-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7002017","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"58c8242a497ee32f1d380f13c30902e71a5c77f82088d71c67f8998400a37571","compact":"50c733dbc97ab33965f6a472d390352e40630e0df7170462ffb89ea7015cd3ca","nasal":"017c708652f458a936ee64062590d976d1b2722beb1c7f1f1dc3e0c8223bfbef"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-2-18","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":2,"verse":18,"english":"But searching for my associates, I had ere this alone repaired to the noble asylum of the Maharși Pulastya of a purified spirit.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.75,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-2-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7002018","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"96c7a9abefd5dc45d9343dbd99a76c5ae334a4d66e46cf6a817cc94bf7b61b5f","compact":"98f2a1c99a76f59fd332c60d36be2142c1996ce9c9f100d5aae729fa45b3cef1","nasal":"98f2a1c99a76f59fd332c60d36be2142c1996ce9c9f100d5aae729fa45b3cef1"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-2-19","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":2,"verse":19,"english":"But associate found there I none, that had come thither. And seeing this change for the worse of my form, I from fear have come hither.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.714,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-2-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7002019","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"1f279788801c809b3f4b8b7110ba745b412597b5ac2e29e7a6bd0b22aeea0fd7","compact":"0335826ab1e168d2cd7aee8734c21fa94e88d843014973fbcc69936efab44dcc","nasal":"0335826ab1e168d2cd7aee8734c21fa94e88d843014973fbcc69936efab44dcc"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-2-20","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":2,"verse":20,"english":"Thereat the Rajarsi, Trinabindu, having a live effulgence through asceticism, entered into contemplation, and saw the consequence of the sage's act.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-2-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7002020","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"27c9da7d6bf961000e92faa12fb37e13fec87b1bffcfd98a7d28a5c672f183bf","compact":"55b300637b7961c18041c7cdbf69058a43675d99aeea8a8588b4b4b3e6193544","nasal":"b13bc3f989b032d20c5105e1cb32e8d105ea575d05c621b321d05125ba168619"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-2-21","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":2,"verse":21,"english":"And coming to know that curse of the Maharși of a purified spirit, he, taking his daughter, went to Pulastya and said.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.831,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-2-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7002021","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"80079ab05faa6946738920c126df1fa0a02fe645ba1d894e092ff5ccffec934b","compact":"272a536